  "title": "A Fano atom acts as one from outside",
  "subject": "How the lines of a Fano atom look to the rest of a three-fold space",
  "conclusion": "In all 277 spaces computed (191 saved, 86 fresh; 1,065 Fano atoms), every atom line outside a Fano atom receives the same far-side vector from each of the atom's lines, though the atom's lines differ on glue lines and in what they receive. On the saved maps the far sides nest: the Fano plane and census 58 create at the same pairs, K4^(3) only where census 6 does, and census 6 without the Fano plane only at glue lines.",
